    "bottomLine": "The best choice for a sound deck that needs a uniform color without the heavy film of paint.",
    "pros": [
      "Thin, flexible film that follows the wood grain texture",
      "Tintable to a wide range of colors",
      "Designed for both decks and siding",
      "Soap-and-water cleanup",
      "Strong reputation among painting contractors"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Sold through Benjamin Moore dealers, not big-box stores",
      "Premium price per gallon",
      "Still needs careful prep and dry wood"
    ],
    "description": "Arborcoat Solid is Benjamin Moore's top waterborne solid stain for exterior wood, and it ranks first because it fits the most common painting job: a structurally sound deck with weathered or mismatched boards that needs an even color. A solid stain like this hides the grain but stays thinner and more flexible than a true paint, so it moves with the wood and keeps the board texture visible. It can be tinted across a wide palette at Benjamin Moore dealers, and the same product works on siding and railings, which makes color matching simple. Owners and contractors commonly describe it as easy to apply evenly with a brush or roller and as aging by gradually wearing in traffic lanes rather than peeling in sheets. It is a premium product with a matching price, roughly 60 to 85 dollars per gallon at the time of writing, and it is only available through dealers. Like every film, it depends on clean, dry, well-prepared wood; it will not save a deck that stays wet."
  },
