            The coating is the last step, not the first. Probe for rot, fix drainage, strip what is failing, coat every edge and let the wood dry. If the grain is still worth seeing, skip paint and look at our <a href="/best-deck-stain-reviews/">deck stain rankings</a> instead; it is far easier to go from stain to paint later than the other way around.
          </p>
